# faces/tallx.t88 - the house 8x8 face, as a selectable .F88 (SPEC.md 6.4)
#
# GENERATED from fonts/tallx.f8 by tools/f8tot88.py - edit the .f8, not this.
#
# Why an 8-ROW face exists in a format built for proportional ones: it is the
# one a document can be set in with NO layout change at all. Every advance is
# 8 and the cell is 8 rows, so Word's row pitch, its caret, its click mapping
# and its wrap are the numbers they already were - only the glyph SHAPES move.
# That makes it the honest first thing a Font menu can offer while SPEC.md
# 65.13's proportional conversion is still unfinished, and it is a real face
# rather than a placeholder: SPEC.md 6.2 records what tallx takes from the
# Macintosh - the enormous lowercase against the capitals, 2-pixel stems for
# the 2.4:1 CGA pixel, square dots, a serifed capital I and narrow figures.

face Tallx
rows 8
ascent 8
leading 0
aspect 0

style regular
psname Courier

